# PTCS Dynamic inline trade marker label renderer

## Pre-work plan

- Background: Daedalus has populated generic `TaMarker` direction, anchor, fill, color, BUY/SELL label, fill price and exit PnL. Renderer currently exposes `Label` only through SVG `<title>`.
- Goal: render bounded visible marker labels beside their K-bar markers, add the Renderer-owned OHLCV data window and shared cursor top timestamp, and preserve existing generic marker/domain boundaries.
- Assumption: `TaMarker.Label` is already the canonical bounded presentation string; Renderer must not parse BUY/SELL/PnL semantics.
- Scope: PTCS Dynamic RFC/current documents, Contracts-compatible Renderer model/view, focused unit tests, browser demo and Playwright visual/interaction gates.
- Invariants: no TradeCore domain fields or producer formatting in PTCS; labels do not affect Y autoscale; pan/zoom keeps marker/label on the same slot; row height and adjacent-row clipping remain stable; SPAA and DIB use the same Renderer path.
- Acceptance: four entry/exit examples render visible text with deterministic lane/clamp behavior; cursor top timestamp and OHLCV window reflect the selected base bar; 4000-bar viewport remains bounded without second-scale pointer work; desktop/mobile browser screenshots and geometry checks pass.
- Risks: label collision/clamping can obscure markers or cross row boundaries; naive per-pointer data scans can regress cursor performance; text measurement must remain deterministic without JavaScript.

